<p>Explanation</p>

<p>The order of synchronous tasks depends on which thread the code line containing <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">dispatch_sync()</code> runs on. If it’s the main thread, the main thread will be blocked waiting for the task to complete. So 1 and 2 are printed first. 3 is printed last because the preceding code block is blocked by the task in the synchronous queue.</p>

